{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/service/ui.go at exact head a5c0889fa3e08f048eb1b09057af26da62ad3882 on request/lane-worktree-identity (pushed), one commit over main 359b211c, clean merge-tree onto current main c0108be8 (tree 8226bc07). The HTTP surface. mainlineRefs is deleted in favour of app.MainlineRefs, so handleLanded and the association's lineage boundary resolve the same mainline from one list. worktreesResponse gains associations, the read-only reverse association table, documented at the field as granting nothing and writing nothing. handleWorktrees runs the association after classification, because a checkout's grade is about which work it claims and its classification is about whether that work is finished: two separate answers, neither an input to the other. The degraded path, where the durable projection is unavailable, now also sets every view's grade to unknown and answers with an empty rows array and a stated reason rather than a missing key, so a reader never sees absence of work where the pass simply did not run. No other endpoint, no authority check and no act path changes.\n\nRewritten at 557ef676 under the second changes-requested verdict 91c50bf9 on 643ab9c5, ratified 2d590023. handleWorktrees now captures one read for the whole request -- one checkout listing, one bounded ref inventory, one remote resolution, one three-second deadline and one 65,536-step budget -- and passes it to both ClassifyCheckouts and AssociateCheckouts, closing it when the request ends. It no longer calls LocalWorktrees and then two independent passes that each read the refs and open a budget of their own. The comment at the call site says what is shared and what is not: the observation and the bound, never the conclusion. The response shape is unchanged, and the degraded path where the durable projection is unavailable still answers with an empty table, a reason and every grade unknown.\n\nSimplified again at e962fa7b under the third changes-requested verdict 5b80e91e on 557ef676, ratified ffd7ffc6: handleWorktrees no longer calls the two judgments itself. It calls AdviseCheckouts, the one response-disposition step, which withholds the whole response when the read did not finish; that is the caller contract this file establishes, and it is the reason the endpoint cannot publish an answer from an unfinished read. The comment at the call site says the three things they share: the observation, the bound, and the whole-response discard when that bound is reached. The response shape is unchanged, and this file is unchanged since e962fa7b. Rests on the app landing artifact for MainlineRefs and on the captured read. Succeeds the live artifacts at this path in the merge target. The artifact at e962fa7b is the outside-target predecessor this head replaces; it is retired separately with this artifact as its successor.","body":{"branch":"request/lane-worktree-identity","commit":"a5c0889fa3e08f048eb1b09057af26da62ad3882","path":"internal/service/ui.go","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2d29fe174fb8255c1c72d2f16590188242944ecd, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:550a2d0c8964b578d81c851516a5aa078b0fc8d3, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a4c569b1cddfb0db72f9239488851f19a291906f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f and 154 more"}}